                <tr id="issuerow12378225" rel="12378225" data-issuekey="CXF-1007" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-1007" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-1007">CXF-1007</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
            <span class="parentIssue">CXF-1004</span>
                Matching resource methods with http method when @HttpMethod annotation does not have name attribute.
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Sub-task</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Invalid
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Jervis Liu
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Jervis Liu
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 14/Sep/07 03:25 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 30/Apr/08 15:01 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 04/Mar/08 19:44 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Section 2.4:<br/>
<br/>
Resource methods are resource class methods annotated with @HttpMethod. They are used to handle <br/>
requests and MUST conform to certain restrictions described in this section. <br/>
The @HttpMethod annotation has an optional value that corresponds to the name of a request method. In <br/>
the absence of a value, the request method is inferred from the resource method name: they match if the <br/>
resource method name starts with the request method name converted to lower case.
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
