                <tr id="issuerow12378374" rel="12378374" data-issuekey="CXF-1026" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-1026" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-1026">CXF-1026</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                multiple-occurence arguments don&#39;t seem to work in tooling argument processing
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Invalid
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Benson Margulies
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Benson Margulies
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 16/Sep/07 17:45 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 04/Dec/09 22:35 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 29/Oct/09 15:56 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Tooling            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-1027                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The command-line parsing system allows for multiple occurences of options in the xml spec for an option. For example:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;option id=&quot;beans&quot; maxOccurs=&quot;unbounded&quot;&gt;<br/>
				&lt;annotation&gt;Specify the pathname of a file defining additional Spring beans to customize databinding<br/>
				configuration.&lt;/annotation&gt;<br/>
				&lt;switch&gt;beans&lt;/switch&gt;<br/>
				&lt;associatedArgument placement=&quot;afterSpace&quot;&gt;<br/>
					&lt;annotation&gt;pathname of the bean definition file.&lt;/annotation&gt;<br/>
				&lt;/associatedArgument&gt;<br/>
			&lt;/option&gt;<br/>
<br/>
However, these don&#39;t seem to really work. By the time the code assembles the HashMap from options to values, any non-first occurences any option are discarded without diagnosis. It seems to me that, if maxOccurs != 1, that the value in the map should be a List&lt;String&gt;, accumulated from the occurences.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
