                <tr id="issuerow12379218" rel="12379218" data-issuekey="CXF-1073" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-1073" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-1073">CXF-1073</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Doc/Lit/Bare with multiple methods with same first param type doesnt work....
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Won&#39;t Fix
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 27/Sep/07 18:25 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 04/Dec/09 22:35 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 15/Oct/09 20:17 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Soap Binding            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">1</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
<br/>
With a doc/lit/bare endpoint, if you have two methods like:<br/>
<br/>
Foo doFoo(AuthToken t, Foo blah);<br/>
Snarf doSnarf(AuthToken t,  Snarf bah);<br/>
<br/>
it doesn&#39;t dispatch correctly.    We only look at the first token when finding the operation.   If we find mulitple operations, we should DOM buffer the whole thing and start looking at the other element names to find the correct operation.<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
