                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      AbstractEndpointFactory &#39;s setServiceName and setEndpointName will not take effect in it createEndpoint() method. <br/>
If we want to set  the service name and endpoint name to the ServerFactoryBean which implement, <br/>
we can walk around it by setting the service name and endpoint name to the ServerFactoryBean&#39;s ServiceFactoryBean member. <br/>
Because we always use ServerFactoryBean and JaxWsServerFactoryBean as Endpoint publish API , <br/>
we need to get the setServiceName and setEndpointName work in the *ServiceFactoryBean.<br/>
<br/>

