                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      If an exception class, declared in &#39;throws&#39; of a JAX-WS interface, has private fields, they get serialized. Not good.
