                <tr id="issuerow12380886" rel="12380886" data-issuekey="CXF-1127" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-1127" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-1127">CXF-1127</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                JAXB Data Binding Generates Duplicate Fault Elements in Generated WSDL
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Ronald Pieterse
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Ronald Pieterse
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 22/Oct/07 08:54 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 05/Dec/07 19:23 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 22/Oct/07 20:18 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAXB Databinding            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      In my service I have 6 calls that can throw 3 exceptions each. In the generated wsdl file the exceptions are all duplicated, times the number of methods. In my case that will be 6 * 3 exception declarations in my wsdl.<br/>
<br/>
Here&#39;s an example of a service method (they all look alike so I did just one):<br/>
<br/>
@WebResult(name = &quot;databaseFields&quot;)<br/>
public DatabaseField[] getDatabaseFields(@WebParam(name = &quot;authInfo&quot;) AuthInfo authInfo, <br/>
                                                                              @WebParam(name = &quot;databaseName&quot;) String databaseName) <br/>
throws InvalidAuthInfoException, InvalidInputException, TripolisUnknownException;<br/>
<br/>
Here&#39;s a snippet from the generated wsdl:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;xsd:schema xmlns:ns0=&quot;http://api.tripolis.com/&quot; xmlns:tns=&quot;http://exceptions.api.tripolis.com/&quot; targetNamespace=&quot;http://exceptions.api.tripolis.com/&quot; attributeFormDefault=&quot;unqualified&quot; elementFormDefault=&quot;unqualified&quot;&gt;<br/>
&lt;xsd:element name=&quot;InvalidAuthInfoException&quot; type=&quot;ns0:invalidAuthInfoFault&quot; nillable=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
&lt;xsd:element name=&quot;TripolisUnknownException&quot; type=&quot;ns0:tripolisUnknownFault&quot; nillable=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
&lt;xsd:element name=&quot;InvalidInputException&quot; type=&quot;ns0:invalidInputFault&quot; nillable=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
&lt;xsd:element name=&quot;InvalidAuthInfoException&quot; type=&quot;ns0:invalidAuthInfoFault&quot; nillable=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
&lt;xsd:element name=&quot;TripolisUnknownException&quot; type=&quot;ns0:tripolisUnknownFault&quot; nillable=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
&lt;xsd:element name=&quot;InvalidInputException&quot; type=&quot;ns0:invalidInputFault&quot; nillable=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
&lt;xsd:element name=&quot;InvalidAuthInfoException&quot; type=&quot;ns0:invalidAuthInfoFault&quot; nillable=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
...<br/>
&lt;xsd:element name=&quot;InvalidAuthInfoException&quot; type=&quot;ns0:invalidAuthInfoFault&quot; nillable=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
&lt;xsd:element name=&quot;TripolisUnknownException&quot; type=&quot;ns0:tripolisUnknownFault&quot; nillable=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
&lt;xsd:element name=&quot;InvalidInputException&quot; type=&quot;ns0:invalidInputFault&quot; nillable=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
&lt;/xsd:schema&gt;<br/>
<br/>
This bug might be the same as https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-745 that was presumed to be fixed.<br/>
<br/>
Am I doing something wrong here? Or was the bug never fixed?
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="labels">    </td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12310060"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12310220">            <span title="22/Oct/07 18:01"><time class="livestamp allow-future" datetime="2007-10-22T18:01:51+0000">22/Oct/07 6:01 PM</time></span>
