</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      WIndows XP<br/>
Java SDK 1.5_0_12
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I modified the apache-cxf-2.0.2-incubator\samples\java_first_jaxws web service to throw a custom exception and a custom request and response object like so:<br/>
<br/>
public interface HelloWorld {<br/>
    Response sayHi(Request text) throws CustomException;<br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
CustomException is a CustomExceptionBase with two string properties. CustomExceptionBase is a java.lang.Exception<br/>
<br/>
The CustomException appears in the WSDL but the CustomExceptionBase is missing. When the service is invoked and throws a CustomException the soap response is:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;soap:Envelope xmlns:soap=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/&quot;&gt;<br/>
   &lt;soap:Body&gt;<br/>
      &lt;soap:Fault&gt;<br/>
         &lt;faultcode&gt;soap:Server&lt;/faultcode&gt;<br/>
         &lt;faultstring&gt;custom error&lt;/faultstring&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/soap:Fault&gt;<br/>
   &lt;/soap:Body&gt;<br/>
&lt;/soap:Envelope&gt;<br/>
<br/>
I am expecting to see the CustomException serialized in the Envelope/Body/Fault/detail node.
  </td>
