</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
Enabling mtom &amp; schema validation for a jaws causes problems once xsd:base64Binary is encountered. It appears that the schema validation is applied to the mtom&#39;d xml which will obviously fail schema validation. To my mind if schema-vallidation &amp; mtom are enabled then schema validation should happen before the mtom step and not after.
