                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      macOSX, java1.5
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I created a test case for elements that are defaulted and use a simpleType is:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;xs:simpleType name=&quot;drivingDecision&quot;&gt;<br/>
    	&lt;xs:restriction base=&quot;xs:string&quot;&gt;<br/>
    		&lt;xs:enumeration value=&quot;RightTurn&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    		&lt;xs:enumeration value=&quot;LeftTurn&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    		&lt;xs:enumeration value=&quot;U-Turn&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    	&lt;/xs:restriction&gt;<br/>
 &lt;/xs:simpleType&gt;<br/>
<br/>
with a line added in complexType &quot;foo&quot;:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;xs:element name=&quot;driving&quot; type=&quot;tns:drivingDecision&quot; default=&quot;LeftTurn&quot; minOccurs=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;/xs:element&gt;<br/>
<br/>
And a test added in DefaultValueTest.java under method: assertDefaultElementValues( Foo foo ):<br/>
<br/>
assertEquals(&quot;Unexpected value for element driving&quot;, &quot;LeftTurn&quot;, foo.getDriving());<br/>

  </td>
