                <tr id="issuerow12383105" rel="12383105" data-issuekey="CXF-1229" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-1229" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-1229">CXF-1229</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Check for element name clash in request and response messages ignores setting of enableWrapperStyle
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Christian Pfeifhofer
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Christian Pfeifhofer
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 23/Nov/07 10:04 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 30/Apr/08 14:54 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 04/Apr/08 01:11 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.6            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Tooling            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-918                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      One way to get around the method signature problems with a request and a response message having an element with the same name but with different datatypes is to disable wrapper style. wsdl2java (of CXF 2.0.2-incubator) ignores the setting of enableWrapperStyle and always fails to generate code in that case, reporting an error:<br/>
<br/>
WSDLToJava Error : Element<br/>
{http://order.rbp.tmobile.at/services/rbpCheckDevices/}data has Having the<br/>
same name with different<br/>
types[{http://order.rbp.tmobile.at/datatypes}RbpCheckDevicesRequestDataType<br/>
-- {http://order.rbp.tmobile.at/datatypes}RbpCheckDevicesResponseDataType],<br/>
In wrapper style, there is a collision as per the spec.<br/>
<br/>
wsdl2java should check for enableWrapperStyle to be true (global and for a specific operation) before checking for name clashes in request and response messages and skip the check otherwise.<br/>

  </td>
