</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Ubuntu Linux
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I&#39;m trying to use Maven to run wsdl2java.  &quot;mvn (phase name)&quot; works fine in generating the classes, but &quot;mvn groupid:artifactid:[version:]goal&quot; returns a &quot;Must specify wsdlOptions&quot; error (even though wsdlOptions are specified).<br/>
<br/>
In particular, placing a hello_world.wsdl file in the src/wsdl directory of a new project, and the attached pom.xml file:<br/>
<br/>
1.) running &quot;mvn generate-sources&quot; has wsdl2java works fine -- artifacts are created.<br/>
<br/>
2.) &quot;mvn org.apache.cxf:cxf-codegen-plugin:wsdl2java&quot;<br/>
or<br/>
&quot;mvn org.apache.cxf:cxf-codegen-plugin:2.0.3-incubator:wsdl2java&quot;,  *fails*, nothing generated, it just returns the &quot;Must specify wsdlOptions&quot; error.<br/>

  </td>
