                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      If I turn on schema validation in CXF in an RPC server, it always fails. This is because JAXB tries to validate the whole input message, and there&#39;s no schema in the wsdl for these things. It seems to me that there could be schema: they are just form-unqualified elements of the elements for the messages. Is there some reason-of-standardization why we can&#39;t just include this in wsdl we generate? If so, we could fabricate it for runtime validation, I guess.<br/>

  </td>
