                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      This issue popped up as part of JAX-WS TCK testing.<br/>
When creating JAX-WS endpoints with no specific address specified a failure occurs due to JettyHttpDestination<br/>
assuming address can never be null.<br/>
The right approach is to allocate a random port at the level of AbstractHttpDestination.<br/>
In fact, it would be easy to extend such solution to handle enterprise policies like :<br/>
&quot;any port withing a given range can be used by endpoints&quot;.<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
