                                            <td class="versions">                        2.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-1415                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Consider the following scenario:<br/>
<br/>
I have a resource with 2 methods:<br/>
<br/>
@HttpMethod(&quot;GET&quot;)<br/>
@UriTemplate(&quot;/users/{id}&quot;)<br/>
@ProduceMime(&quot;text/xml&quot;)<br/>
public Response getUser(@UriParam(&quot;id&quot;) String id) throws Exception { ....}<br/>
<br/>
@HttpMethod(&quot;GET&quot;)<br/>
@UriTemplate(&quot;/users/{id}&quot;)<br/>
@ProduceMime(&quot;application/json&quot;)<br/>
public Response getUserJSON(@UriParam(&quot;id&quot;) String id) throws Exception { ....}<br/>
<br/>
If I then send a request to /users/24 with Accept headers of  &quot;text/xml, */*&quot; one would expect the &quot;text/xml&quot; method to be invoked. However in the CXF implementation the application/json one is invoked. Suggest changing the algorithm to:<br/>
<br/>
1. Sort the Accept header according to the W3 standards<br/>
2. Iterate through the accept header list. For each one:<br/>
        1. Find all matching methods<br/>
        2. If there is only one method return this and break out of the accept header loop<br/>
        3. If there are multiple methods sort these methods using consume mime and produce mime. Then return the first<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
