                <tr id="issuerow12394117" rel="12394117" data-issuekey="CXF-1533" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-1533" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-1533">CXF-1533</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Clients generated with CXF from java using Aegis DataBinding and SimpleFrontEnd sends the header SoapAction empty. This prevent interaction with oracle soa products wich depends on this header to execute correctly.
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Benson Margulies
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Simon Paredes
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Simon Paredes
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 16/Apr/08 15:31 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 03/Jul/08 17:19 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 02/May/08 22:54 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.5            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.1.1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Aegis Databinding            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      it could be added to org.apache.cxf.service.factory.DefaultServiceConfiguration this implementation of the function getAction():<br/>
<br/>
public String getAction(OperationInfo op, Method method) {<br/>
        String action = op.getName().getLocalPart();<br/>
        if(StringUtils.isEmpty(action)){<br/>
        	action = method.getName();<br/>
        }<br/>
        return action;<br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
Wich is a first aproach, of course, but for the simple case it works.<br/>
<br/>
Actually org.apache.cxf.service.factory.DefaultServiceConfiguration has no implementation for getAction and org.apache.cxf.service.factory.AbstractServiceConfiguration returns null.
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
