                <tr id="issuerow12394340" rel="12394340" data-issuekey="CXF-1536" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-1536" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-1536">CXF-1536</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                When a SOAP request is submitted without an enclosing &lt;/soapenv:Envelope&gt; a successful response is returned.  I would think that this should generate a parsing error/exception.
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Bob Dellago
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Bob Dellago
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 18/Apr/08 19:52 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 04/Dec/09 22:34 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 05/Nov/09 18:07 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.2.5            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Soap Binding            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">1</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows 2003<br/>
Jboss 4.2.1GA<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      When a SOAP request is submitted without an enclosing &lt;/soapenv:Envelope&gt; a successful response is returned.  I would think that this should generate a parsing error/exception.<br/>
<br/>
&lt;soapenv:Envelope xmlns:soapenv=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/&quot; xmlns:v1=&quot;http://www.nortel.com/xmlprotocol/wsdl/protocol_interfaces/v1_0/&quot;&gt;<br/>
   &lt;soapenv:Header/&gt;<br/>
   &lt;soapenv:Body&gt;<br/>
      &lt;v1:CallCleared-Event&gt;<br/>
         &lt;!--Optional:--&gt;<br/>
         &lt;callId&gt;1-1-1-1&lt;/callId&gt;<br/>
         &lt;cause&gt;6&lt;/cause&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/v1:CallCleared-Event&gt;<br/>
   &lt;/soapenv:Body&gt;<br/>
*** missing soapenv ***<br/>
<br/>
Actual Response:<br/>
&lt;soap:Envelope xmlns:soap=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/&quot;&gt;<br/>
   &lt;soap:Body&gt;<br/>
      &lt;ns1:CallCleared-EventResponse xmlns:ns1=&quot;http://www.nortel.com/xmlprotocol/wsdl/protocol_interfaces/v1_0/&quot;&gt;<br/>
         &lt;status&gt;success&lt;/status&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/ns1:CallCleared-EventResponse&gt;<br/>
   &lt;/soap:Body&gt;<br/>
&lt;/soap:Envelope&gt;<br/>

  </td>
