    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-1590" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-1590">CXF-1590</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Quoted-Printable Content-Transfer-Encoding does not get decoded
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            aaron pieper
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            aaron pieper
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 16/May/08 16:36 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 24/Apr/09 21:16 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 12/Mar/09 20:37 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.10,                     2.1.4            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-1847                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The following is an MTOM attachment generated by SoapUI, a web testing tool:<br/>
<br/>
------=_Part_6_1979395.1210796510882<br/>
Content-Type: text/xml; charset=Cp1252<br/>
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable<br/>
Content-ID: 606517570647<br/>
<br/>
&lt;?xml version=3D&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=3D&quot;UTF-8&quot;?&gt;<br/>
&lt;MyXml attribute=3D&quot;value&quot;&gt;<br/>
&lt;/MyXml&gt;<br/>
<br/>
The content-transfer-encoding is quoted-printable, and the attachment uses &quot;=3D&quot; throughout, which is a quoted-printable-encoded equals sign. CXF should handle the decoding of this attachment. However, when this attachment reaches my web service implementation after going through CXF&#39;s interceptors, the &quot;=3D&quot; characters are still included the document, rendering the XML invalid.
