                <tr id="issuerow12396803" rel="12396803" data-issuekey="CXF-1609" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-1609" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-1609">CXF-1609</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                The setSynchronousTimeout on the ClientImpl does not prevent reading the socket to timeout...
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Benjamin Coiffe
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Benjamin Coiffe
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 26/May/08 10:18 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 03/Jul/08 17:19 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 16/Jun/08 17:46 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.1.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.1.1,                     2.0.7            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Configuration,                     Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      This method has apparently been replaced with<br/>
    HTTPConduit.setReceiverTimeout(Long). <br/>
    HTTPConduit.setConnectionTimeout(Long)<br/>
I can&#39;t remember how the old way was meant to work (private void ClientImpl.waitForResponse(...)) but this seems to be deprecated atm.<br/>
<br/>
Other thing:<br/>
        HTTPConduit.setReceiverTimeout(Long)<br/>
        HTTPConduit.setConnectionTimeout(Long)<br/>
are casted as int in the conduit :<br/>
        connection.setConnectTimeout((int)clientSidePolicy.getConnectionTimeout());<br/>
        connection.setReadTimeout((int)clientSidePolicy.getReceiveTimeout());<br/>
<br/>
This conversion is very dangerous e.g Long.MAX_VALUE is converted into a negative integer!<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
