                <tr id="issuerow12399106" rel="12399106" data-issuekey="CXF-1670" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-1670" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-1670">CXF-1670</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                CXF circular recursion issues when Marshalling Hibernate Objects
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Won&#39;t Fix
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Antoine E. Hall
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Antoine E. Hall
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 26/Jun/08 18:16 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 30/Jul/09 17:59 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 11/Jul/09 11:28 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">1</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      FC 8<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I&#39;m using CXF with Spring/Hibernate wiring and support.  I have an object that makes a reference to another and this works fine outside of CXF.  When I attempt to use a client to access the ws, it fails with the errors shown below.  Is there a way to limit CXF from making recursive calls?<br/>
<br/>
The hibernate object looks something like:<br/>
<br/>
public class A {<br/>
  private String something;<br/>
  private List&lt;B&gt; Bs = new ArrayList&lt;B&gt;(0);<br/>
  ...<br/>
  @OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL, fetch = FetchType.LAZY, mappedBy = &quot;athing&quot;)<br/>
  @Cascade({org.hibernate.annotations.CascadeType.ALL, org.hibernate.annotations.CascadeType.DELETE_ORPHAN})<br/>
   public List&lt;B&gt; getB() {<br/>
        return this.Bs;<br/>
   }<br/>
   ...<br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
public class B {<br/>
   private String otherthing;<br/>
   private A athing;<br/>
   ...<br/>
   @ManyToOne(fetch = FetchType.LAZY)<br/>
   @OnDelete(action = org.hibernate.annotations.OnDeleteAction.CASCADE)<br/>
   @JoinColumn(name = &quot;country_id&quot;, nullable = false)<br/>
    public A getA() {<br/>
	return this.athing;<br/>
    }<br/>
   ...<br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
Jun 26, 2008 12:40:38 PM org.apache.catalina.core.StandardWrapperValve invoke<br/>
SEVERE: Servlet.service() for servlet CXFServlet threw exception<br/>
java.lang.StackOverflowError<br/>
