                <tr id="issuerow12401494" rel="12401494" data-issuekey="CXF-1731" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-1731" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-1731">CXF-1731</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Unexpected control based on the namespace of the soap:body element
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Stéphane ARDOUIN
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Stéphane ARDOUIN
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 01/Aug/08 14:21 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 13/Nov/09 17:27 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 28/Oct/09 20:36 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.8            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.2.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Soap Binding            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      It appears that CXF and/or JAXB interprets the attribute &lt;soap:body namespace&gt; of the WSDL as a control to apply on the namespace.<br/>
For a schema without &quot;elementForm=Qualified&quot; elements, there shouldn&#39;t be such control. <br/>
<br/>
This ticket is based on the thread &quot;Different behaviors between Axis and CXF for namespaces&quot; on 2008/07/29, ending with the following comment of Daniel Kulp :<br/>
The namespace on the soap:body thing is really just used for Rpc/ <br/>
Lit.   In that case, the runtime needs to create a new wrapper element  <br/>
which is the operation name plus that namespace.   For doc/lit which  <br/>
everything is completely controlled by the elements in the namespace, it should be irrelevant.<br/>

  </td>
