</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      when using a custom jaxb binding file, when &lt;jaxb:javadoc&gt; is used on a property, the javadoc should be created on the field, not on the getter of the field.  Here&#39;s an example of the binding file:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;jaxb:bindings node=&quot;xs:complexType[@name=&#39;myComplexType&#39;]&quot;&gt;<br/>
  &lt;jaxb:bindings node=&quot;/xs:complexContent/xs:extension/xs:sequence/xs:element[@name=&#39;myField&#39;]&quot;&gt;<br/>
    &lt;jaxb:property&gt;<br/>
      &lt;jaxb:javadoc&gt;<br/>
        &lt;![CDATA[this comment should appear on the field, not the getter of the field]]&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/jaxb:javadoc&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/jaxb:property&gt; <br/>
  &lt;/jaxb:bindings&gt;	<br/>
&lt;/jaxb:bindings&gt;<br/>

  </td>
