                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      If my SOAP service returns a String that contains control characters and the service is consumed by a CXF client a com.ctc.wstx.exc.WstxUnexpectedCharException is being thrown.<br/>
<br/>
It&#39;s easy to duplicate (in my setup) by modifying one line of the CXF 2.1.2 sample samples/java_first_jaxws:<br/>
<br/>
    public String sayHiToUser(User user) {<br/>
        System.out.println(&quot;sayHiToUser called&quot;);<br/>
        users.put(users.size() + 1, user);<br/>
        return &quot;Hello &quot;  + user.getName() + &#39;\27&#39;;          &lt;&lt;&lt;===== add &#39;\27&#39; to the String being returned<br/>
    }<br/>
<br/>
Now when you start the client sample the following exception is being thrown:<br/>
<br/>
