                <tr id="issuerow12403482" rel="12403482" data-issuekey="CXF-1778" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-1778" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-1778">CXF-1778</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Memory leak occurs in specific cases when WS-Addressing feature is enabled
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Critical
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Maciej Kwiecien
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Maciej Kwiecien
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 01/Sep/08 10:40 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 23/Oct/08 03:59 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 03/Sep/08 18:21 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.1.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.1.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        WS-* Components            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I observed memory leak  (OOM thrown) in following situations:<br/>
<br/>
1.WS-Addressing enabled on client and server side. When server stops responding (connection refused on client side) <br/>
client memory usage is increasing until OOM is thrown.<br/>
<br/>
2.WS-Addressing enabled only on client side, server provide service without WS-Addressing feature (or WS-Addressing configuration is incorrect). Client memory  heap is building up even faster than in first case.<br/>
<br/>
I will provide a sample application and more detailed description how to reproduce bug.<br/>

  </td>
