                                            <td class="environment">      RHEL 4.x
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      wsdl2java utility throws exception on naming collision.  I&#39;ve isolated which part of the WSDL causes this error.  Using the below &lt;schema&gt; excerpt, the tool will through the exception referenced in the title of this issue.<br/>
<br/>
wsdl excerpt:<br/>
<br/>
 &lt;wsdl:types&gt;<br/>
        &lt;xsd:schema ...&gt;<br/>
            &lt;xsd:element name=&quot;accountID&quot;&gt;<br/>
                &lt;xsd:simpleType&gt;<br/>
                    &lt;xsd:restriction base=&quot;xsd:string&quot;/&gt;<br/>
                &lt;/xsd:simpleType&gt;<br/>
            &lt;/xsd:element&gt;<br/>
            &lt;xsd:complexType name=&quot;Account&quot;&gt;<br/>
                &lt;xsd:sequence&gt;<br/>
                    &lt;xsd:element minOccurs=&quot;0&quot; name=&quot;ID&quot; nillable=&quot;true&quot; type=&quot;xsd:string&quot;/&gt;                   <br/>
                &lt;/xsd:sequence&gt;<br/>
            &lt;/xsd:complexType&gt;<br/>
        &lt;/xsd:schema&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/wsdl:types&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Seems there is some issue when an element &#39;accountID&#39; and an element &#39;Account&#39; with a sub element &#39;ID&#39; are both present.  The following exception is thrown:<br/>
<br/>
WSDLToJava Error: Thrown by JAXB : Two declarations cause a collision in the ObjectFactory class.<br/>
<br/>

