</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Hi, <br/>
I have a web service which accepts a byte parameter in one of the objects and aegis does not support it out of the box.  I ran across this issue submitted to XFire some time ago, but it seems it was never fixed:<br/>
<br/>
http://jira.codehaus.org/browse/XFIRE-462<br/>
<br/>
That bug focuses mainly on the wsdl creation, but the byte values don&#39;t even get passed correctly to the service.  It seems like a pretty simple fix,so I&#39;m not really sure why it was never resolved.  For the time being I added some custom types (basically just like the ShortType) to handle the two byte classes, but things would be a lot cleaner if aegis supported them.<br/>
<br/>
Preferably, this would be resolved in the 2.0.x branch as we have not yet moved to 2.1.x.
  </td>
