</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      This issue occurs when generating the WSDL from a Java class.  See the following code<br/>
<br/>
private Integer zOrder;<br/>
<br/>
public Integer getZOrder() { return this.zOrder; }<br/>
<br/>
public void setZOrder(final Integer zOrder) { this.zOrder = zOrder; }<br/>
<br/>
The above code will generate the following WSDL snippet:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;xs:element minOccurs=&quot;0&quot; name=&quot;ZOrder&quot; nillable=&quot;true&quot; type=&quot;xs:int&quot;/&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Notice the capital Z.  Based on other behavior, I would expect that the WSDL would look like:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;xs:element minOccurs=&quot;0&quot; name=&quot;zOrder&quot; nillable=&quot;true&quot; type=&quot;xs:int&quot;/&gt;<br/>

  </td>
