                <tr id="issuerow12412305" rel="12412305" data-issuekey="CXF-1978" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-1978" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-1978">CXF-1978</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Spring-based JMS Conduit should support using a shared permanent reply queue for several instances
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Christian Schneider
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Ron Gavlin
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Ron Gavlin
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 13/Jan/09 17:15 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 09/Feb/09 22:19 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 21/Jan/09 20:37 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.9,                     2.1.3            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.10,                     2.1.4            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Transports            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">1</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The new Spring-based JMS Conduit should support using a shared permanent reply queue for several instances. The problem with temporary replyTo queues is that it is difficult to semantically associate the temporary replyTo queues with their original &quot;request&quot; queues. Using a named replyTo queue with a selector based on the correlationId solves this problem. This may be considered a &quot;regression&quot; introduced during the upgrade from CXF 2.1.2 to 2.1.3.<br/>
<br/>
See Nabble Thread http://www.nabble.com/forum/ViewPost.jtp?post=20447067&amp;framed=y.<br/>
<br/>
/Ron
  </td>
