                <tr id="issuerow12413148" rel="12413148" data-issuekey="CXF-2002" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2002" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2002">CXF-2002</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Server async jms transport needs dynamic mechanism to throttle message consumption
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Ron Gavlin
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Ron Gavlin
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 24/Jan/09 04:15 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 03/Aug/09 20:06 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 28/Jul/09 18:04 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.9,                     2.1.3,                     2.0.10            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.1.6,                     2.2.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Transports            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently, the server-side async jms transport has no mechanism to throttle consumption of incoming messages. This becomes problematic in scenarios where a large backlog of messages exists on the input queue. In this case, it is likely that the cxf server will overload its internal work item queues resulting in problems. A dynamic throttling mechanism on the async jms server is required to avoid this problem.
