                <tr id="issuerow12413524" rel="12413524" data-issuekey="CXF-2013" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2013" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2013">CXF-2013</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                CXF Server with ASYNC jms transport should support pluggable StoreFactory abstraction (memory &amp; jdbc) to manage continuations
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> New Feature</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Won&#39;t Fix
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Ron Gavlin
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Ron Gavlin
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 29/Jan/09 11:13 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 26/Oct/11 17:12 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 09/Sep/11 18:39 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.9            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Transports            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I am using the CXF Server with JMS transport embedded in async smx cxf-bc:consumer as a bridge to a back-end system that accepts large numbers of request, each of which tends to run for long periods of time. So, it is not practical for the continuations in the CXF Server to be stored in memory. Rather, these should be stored in a database shared by a cluster of servers.<br/>
<br/>
This is a request to enhance CXF to optionally inject &quot;StoreFactory&quot; implementations into JMSDestination which currently holds the list of CXF Continuations directly in memory.<br/>

  </td>
