                <tr id="issuerow12413563" rel="12413563" data-issuekey="CXF-2014" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-2014" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2014">CXF-2014</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                @Path fails when uses variable with regexp containing curly braces.
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Andrzej Michalec
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Andrzej Michalec
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Andrzej Michalec
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 29/Jan/09 21:34 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 14/Apr/09 17:59 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 14/Apr/09 17:51 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.2.1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      According to JAX-RS spec 1.0 one can use @Path annotation that specifies regular expression to match variable content. Most of regexps work fine e.g. @Path(&quot;{var:[a-zA-Z]+}&quot;), however use of curly braces in regexp causes failure of JAX-RS in runtime e.g. this @Path(&quot;{var:\d{2,}}&quot;) fails.<br/>
From first look on URITemplate class responsible for URI regexps, its internal matcher treats first closing curly brace as ending of whole expression.<br/>
<br/>
cheers,<br/>
andy
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
